  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regular Resources for Development Interventions in Eswatini</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regular Resources, commonly referred to as TRAC (Target for Resource Assignment from the Core) funds, serve as the backbone of UNDP Eswatini&#x2019;s development programming. Their primary purpose is to provide flexible, predictable, and non-earmarked financing that enables the Country Office to respond strategically to national priorities and emerging challenges.In essence, TRAC funds are the strategic enabler that ensures UNDP Eswatini can deliver on its mandate with agility, resilience, and impact-bridging gaps, sustaining momentum, and reinforcing the organization&#x2019;s role as a trusted development partner.</narrative>
  </description>
